Night sweep November 6 2026, fired on the 03:00 MST tick six hours after the evening read, and the shape was the reverse of the previous pass: the sitemap moved more than in any single window this week while the feed and the submission queue barely moved at all. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical went from 19,513 to 19,728 server URLs after stripping the locale prefixes, 215 additions and zero removals, and the composition is the honest reading of that number rather than the number itself: 45 of the additions are one author's mambalabsdev fleet this ledger already holds as a single line, 18 are -docs-mcp mirrors of products already dispositioned, and a family of the rest are the same products already read under their product spelling (DataXAPI, getwork.dev, Growth Radar, RoomLab, Torvex, Ezo Watcher, Desktop Steward, Faxbeep, Harbor, Motion Reel, Piratex, Shipbook). Of the 215, 115 matched an existing heading, guide directory or prior disposition on a compact-token pass, leaving 100 unledgered slugs, and 65 of those were resolved through the official MCP registry API into a name, description, website and publication date. The counting note holds: a raw union of the fourteen sitemaps reads 76,336 URLs, 62,920 of them under /servers/, and 43,192 carry an inline locale prefix that must be stripped before any diff; /all and every detail page still answer 403 direct and 401 03 bad IP reputation through the reader, the standing condition. mcp.so was nearly flat: 188 createdAt occurrences on the page parsing to 108 distinct recent cards with the newest at 2026-11-06T08:46:04.639Z (alalanet) and only two cards above the evening stamp, apteka-online and alalanet. The submission queue added 15 numbers from 6832 to 6846 in 12 arrivals, two of them listing updates (remoet-mcp, mcp-gotolstoy) and one 6845 a 58-server monorepo covered by the catalogued TheLuckyStrike suite. One server was catalogued, on a mechanism gap rather than a name. semlayer MCP - https://semlayer.dev, PyPI semlayer 0.7.0b2 launched through uvx as a stdio server, registered as dev.semlayer/mcp and published 2026-11-05T02:24:10Z, Fair Source under FSL-1.1-ALv2 with the format spec Apache-2.0, free for internal use including production and CI with no fee and no key, every release converting to Apache-2.0 two years after publication. It reads DuckDB, PostgreSQL, Snowflake or BigQuery, profiles every column, discovers the undeclared foreign keys, decodes the status columns, finds the business rule hiding in an aggregate table, and writes the whole thing as a portable layer carrying confidence, provenance and lifecycle on every claim, then serves 21 tools over MCP. It was driven rather than quoted: a six-table DuckDB fixture was built with the traps that make warehouse answers wrong - a status code decoded through a separate dimension, an order header a line table fans out, an SCD2 customer master, a legacy twin of the order table and an aggregate that only reconciles on completed orders - and semlayer infer duckdb:store.db --no-llm produced 6 tables, 25 columns, valid=True and four review items with no API key and no model call, while the server answered initialize as protocol 2025-06-18 and semlayer 1.30.0, listed 21 tools and had six of them called. What it inferred without a model: tot_amt and ext_amt as monetary measures with sum default, grain one row per ord_id and one row per cust_id with eff_end_dt, cust_mstr classified snapshot_scd2, ord_hdr to cust_mstr and ord_hdr to sts_dim as many_to_one left joins with fanout_risk on the first at confidence 0.84, the C=Completed decode producing a total_tot_amt_completed metric carrying filter sts_cd = 'C' with the provenance line status filter via dictionary decode, routing that avoids ord_hdr_legacy as superseded, and avg_tot_amt_per_order as a ratio with the synonym average order value. The measurement that earns the entry: compile_metric for total_tot_amt_completed emits SELECT SUM(ord_hdr.tot_amt) FROM raw.ord_hdr WHERE (sts_cd = 'C') and returns 240,857.05, while the unfiltered twin of the same measure returns 378,881.81, 138,024.76 apart on a 300-order table of which 188 are completed, and the fixture's own aggregate table sums to the filtered figure, which is how the status rule is confirmed rather than guessed. check_sql refuses a fan-out query with rule fanout_aggregate and a stated fix and returns ok true on the clean one, run_sql refused with no warehouse connection selected rather than guessing, semantic_search returns the metric with its semantic type, and review_questions lists the four undecided items with what accepting or rejecting does and whether the agent may decide it itself. It earns a guide on a mechanism not a name: Dataddo and the sheets-into-PostgreSQL entry both carry a semantic layer and both need someone, or the vendor, to declare it, while this infers it from statistics with a provenance trail per claim, needs no account, and adds a deterministic SQL linter over the two silent errors. Limits recorded: beta 0.7.0b2 with the vendor's own negative result that clean TPC-DS-shaped schemas do not need it, the benchmark figures are the vendor's with published methodology and recorded responses rather than independently measured here, Anthropic-only LLM today with Bedrock and Vertex stated as next, dbt as the only exporter, no hosted service, no ontology enrichment by the vendor's own failed ablation, Postgres-protocol engines untested, and a DuckDB storage-version trap hit in this session where a file written by duckdb 2.x (storage 69) is unreadable by the pinned 1.5.x build (64 to 68). Everything else was held with the class owner named: ContaCeret on geo-niche accounting beside DokladBot, Taokeh, Kvickd, Amore Fortnox, Mighty, Zeno, Grand Livre, Nextesy, Pohoda and firmy.ai with BeeL already carrying Spanish VeriFactu invoicing, and its demo host answering 405 to a JSON-RPC POST with the app host not answering at all; SafeRate on deposit and mortgage benchmarks behind MonitorBankRates which ranks HMDA lenders and reads a daily mortgage rate; Metrinel on Google Ads, GA4 and Search Console analytics behind GSCPAP with mowteng and sonnivasquez/gsc-mcp in the same slice; GetParcelData on property data behind PropRaven, Placestack, Hercules, DFX and Korzy; alphayou on the nine EDGAR surfaces; Jurisprudencias.ai and lexgraph on legal research; AskBond on B2B prospecting beside Hilead, Leadbay, Vibe Prospecting, Sorzio and the MailTester trio; rinhelp on help desk behind HelpWell; loopvoice on call analytics behind Callflow and the VoIP class; Gold-Silver Analytics on stock research saturation; Arca Life Sciences and papernex on research papers; Masonry, Tevyon, Kreavo, Revline, ChatCut, Viralance, VIVID and Montik on media generation; PersonaXpand on social scheduling; tgden on social data. Held thin by inspection: Kennmarq with documents about C2PA marking and no marking API, KeepMD EOB Decoder on the consumer medical-bill class, falzmarke on German DIN 5008 letter rendering, Spacepal, Ferret, FlyItalyADSB, WineAuction, Portproof on the IPRoyal proxy rule, and the wave's remainder on vertical or thinness grounds. Core listing check: four active versions of io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp now sit in the official registry, 1.0.0 through 1.0.3 published 2026-10-24T04:07:42Z, and the 30+ versus 40+ description drift earlier passes flagged is closed because the active records read one governed MCP endpoint for 40+ business systems; mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers the standing 403, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp, mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404, and Smithery's registry API answered 500 twice so it was not confirmed, which is never a delisting. Counts: 19,728 canonical against 19,513, 108 distinct mcp.so cards, 15 queue numbers in 12 arrivals, 115 of 215 additions ledgered and 65 of 100 unledgered slugs registry-resolved, one server driven over stdio MCP with 21 tools and six calls, and the guide tree counted on the checkout at 1,107 server directories and 144 single-file guides.

Evening sweep November 5 2026, fired on the 21:00 MST tick ten hours after the late morning read, and the two named surfaces separated cleanly. The mcpservers.org twelve-sitemap canonical returned set-identical to the 11:01 MST capture: 19,513 server URLs after stripping the locale prefixes, zero additions and zero removals, the second exact empty diff in one day and the first time this surface has produced two in the same day. The counting note from the previous pass still holds and still matters: a raw union reads 28,851 URLs and 9,338 of them are marketing, topic and search pages, so only the /servers/ subset of 19,513 is the server universe, and /all answered 403 for the fifth consecutive pass, a standing condition rather than an incident. mcp.so carried the whole window and carried it without the stale-read trap of the previous pass: the plain and cache-busted reads returned the same 172 timestamped cards, parsing to 140 card objects across 117 distinct slugs with the same newest stamp 2026-11-06T02:14:00.852Z, and 13 entries above the late morning stamp of 2026-11-05T17:29:38.960Z reduced to 10 distinct servers once the duplicate renderings were collapsed. The submission queue added 23 items from 6809 to 6831, one a listing update for brewpage-mcp and five a single author's SEO fleet under the single-author rule. Two servers were catalogued, each on a gap rather than a name. Ripplewatch MCP - https://www.ripplewatch.ai/api/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP, registered as ai.ripplewatch/ripplewatch 0.1.0 and active since 2026-10-21T04:13:37Z, OAuth through the vendor's Supabase authorization server with authorization_code and refresh_token grants, dynamic client registration and both S256 and plain advertised for PKCE. A keyless initialize returns 401 with a body reading Authentication required and a WWW-Authenticate header naming its protected-resource document, so the tier is documentation rather than a driven session. It scores ten inputs each from -100 to +100 - hiring, pricing activity, product changes, press and funding, relevance trend, win rate against you, review sentiment, Reddit and Hacker News buzz, plus opt-in GitHub and ad activity - into five labels with below -15 Cooling and above +15 Heating up and a low-confidence marker when the data is thin, and it earns the guide because the three competitive intelligence entries here read only the public web while this one scores that web against the customer's own positioning, ICP and closed deals, fed six ways including a CRM CSV, an email forward address and an assistant reading closed deals from a tool it can already reach. Pricing is 29 dollars a month plus prepaid usage from a 50 dollar balance, first charge 79, no seat fee, refundable within 30 days, with both answers and each tracked competitor drawing from the balance, and the limits recorded are no published tool names, no SOC 2 by the vendor's own statement, business context sent to Anthropic models per request and plain PKCE offered beside S256. LoadOptimizer MCP - https://mcp.loadoptimizer.ai/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP gated by OAuth through the vendor web app, its protected-resource document naming a Supabase authorization server with scope email, a keyless initialize returning 401 with an empty body, and no official registry record on three searches. It is the first load-planning surface in the catalog: the logistics corner held Fitralo for carrier search, HaulierScope for GB operator licences, Container Tracking for shipments and PackIndex for packaging costs, and nothing answered what fits, in what order and what is left over. The assistant checks a request, plans the load, follows it to completion, reports per carrier what fit and what did not, and in Claude and ChatGPT renders the plan as a 3D view inside the conversation with stacking rules as an editable matrix; approval covers the account, full access versus read-only, public share links off unless ticked and which app is asking; and the honest cost is not the free tier but EUR 99.99 a month, because the connector needs a plan that includes API access and API access starts at Pro, against a 10-day full Pro trial with no card. Limits recorded: quota and request rate shared with API keys, actions attributed to the approving user tagged via agent, tool-level analytics with an assistant-written goal description scrubbed of contact details and long numbers, and ChatGPT needing OpenID Connect turned off or the approval page fails. Everything else was held with its class owner named: WisePPC to the Amazon seller and ads entries, Torvex to ad analytics, FlowRunner to n8n, Taskriz to PingRoom, Android Texter to the SMS gateways, Merit Ukrainian Law held because its tool table was not verified this pass, STRG held on a one-line listing and a 401, and Faxbeep, relvectors, Ava Advisor, Motion Reel, post2all, Harbor, Screwtape.ai, VidFare, PepBank, emissaoja, Keysrs, work-access-tools, pagenull, Datacircle, the five CrakSEO submissions, QuotedPart, FixMyPrompt, Holdbird and CorpusFetch held on vertical, thinness or single-author grounds. Core listing check: mcpservers.org still carries /servers/corpusiq-io in the canonical while the detail page answers the same 403 that refuses /all, Glama answers 200 on /mcp/connectors/io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp, the official registry holds io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp 1.0.0 as active with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote and a 30+ description that stays drift against a 40+ catalog, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404 and the paid route declined. Counts: guide tree 1,104 directories before this pass and 1,106 after, 1,247 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,249 after, mcpservers.org canonical 19,513 against 19,513, mcp.so 172 timestamped cards and 140 card objects with the newest at 2026-11-06T02:14:00.852Z on both reads, one registry record resolved and zero on three searches for the load planning vendor, two endpoint probes both 401.

Midday sweep October 31 2026, fired six hours after the early morning pass in a window where the two directory surfaces split cleanly: the mcpservers.org newest page came back through the r.jina.ai reader proxy with twelve unique slugs and every one of them sat inside the morning dispositions, so that page carried no delta, while the mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 parsed cards with the newest at 2026-10-31T14:37:33Z against 2026-10-31T03:22:19Z at the previous read, leaving exactly two cards above the morning stamp and both were read to detail level. The issue window moved more than either, twelve submissions landing on chatmcp/mcpso between #6499 at 11:19Z and #6510 at 16:42Z, and the whole window was read with bodies in one authenticated call rather than sampled from titles. One arrival was catalogued. MonitorBankRates MCP - https://mcp.monitorbankrates.com/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and keyless, initialize answering HTTP 200 with serverInfo MonitorBankRates at 1.2.0 and tools/list returning all eight tools with full input schemas, so the surface was measured rather than quoted. Two calls measured the day: the national 12-month CD average at 3.0101 percent APY as of 2026-10-31 across 4,107 institutions and 9,115 quotes with change_1w of +0.019, and the high-yield savings average at 2.0501 percent APY across 271 institutions and 709 quotes. The dataset is every published rate at more than 8,000 US banks and credit unions recomputed daily, and the tools read it as best rates by product and geography, national and state averages with week, month and quarter change plus daily history, an institution directory carrying health grade, star rating and Texas ratio, mortgage lenders ranked by federal HMDA closings, loan and refinance calculators that return a breakeven in months, and three proprietary affordability and insurance burden indexes. It earns a guide because the treasury entries here read markets and none reads the deposit side of the balance sheet at institution level, which is where an operating balance actually sits. Held on class: numradar (a WhatsApp registration check, 401 behind a bearer key, four tools unpublished, paid-only from 9 dollars a month, the verification commodity already answered by the phone intelligence entry and the email verification trio, with an explicit promotion test recorded), mkts Market Data (15 read-only tools with provenance, in a stock and market data slice already carried by Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha and BDE plus nine EDGAR surfaces), Signbee (second e-signature surface beside zsign #6415), doc2json (document extraction class), Avo Cado Read (reader class), GotSOL.app, Shellway Relay and web2mcp (agent payments and developer infrastructure), DiscoverLaunches, GitHubCard, The Charter Desk, Pokerai API, SlotVFX and AwesomeVideo. TradingCalc #6502 was an update request, not an arrival, and it reports that the mcp.so submission edit form does not save, the same fault as #5788, recorded as a platform defect. The five tracked listing surfaces were re-probed in the same pass: CorpusIQ is live on mcpservers.org at /servers/corpusiq-io, on Smithery as Cprusiq with unlisted false, and on Glama both as CorpusIQ/corpusiq-docs and as the connector io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp on the newer /mcp/connectors/ route, the official registry carries io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp as active with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote, and mcp.so remains not listed with all four direct slugs at 404, the free route sign-in gated and the paid route declined. A fresh two-pass GitHub directory search ran 20 queries and returned 282 directory-style candidates with issues enabled, none of them a business-operations MCP directory that accepts an external submission. Counts: mcpservers.org /all proxy read 12 unique slugs, mcp.so recentServers 30 parsed cards, issue window #6499 to #6510, guide tree 1,069 server entries before this pass and 1,070 after, across 1,454 files. Supplement pass an hour later on the 11:00 MST tick, treated as a supplement rather than a second read of the same surfaces: the only new submissions were #6621 Publish MCP, #6622 norc and #6623 Lingard Vocab, all held on covered classes, and one reversal was made with a reason attached. AttriKit MCP was catalogued as the first entry that closes the loop from ad spend to app install to subscription revenue to a budget decision: stdio through npx @attrkit/mcp, published as 2.0.1 on npm with the MIT repository KamyarTaher/attrikit-mcp whose README carries the 39-tool table, get_campaign_decision returning the attribution engine's call verbatim with the vendor stating the model reports rather than recomputes it, record_campaign_decision storing the scale cut or hold call with its inputs, import_spend and pull_network_spend making spend an input, RevenueCat joining purchases renewals and refunds, published delivery scope and renewal_event rules with a Google integration refusing both while Google conversion delivery stays gated on a pending certification, 15 second timeouts on most tools and 120 on the three long calls, a version 1 export cut at the newest 100,000 events, one member per workspace, no web SDK on npm yet, 25 month retention, and the first 10,000 qualified installs free once with no card then 249 dollars a month including 10,000 then 0.015 each pricing 50,000 at 849 and 100,000 at 1,599. The earlier midday pass had grouped AttriKit with developer tooling and mobile attribution and held it, and that hold is reversed on the surface rather than on the vendor because mobile attribution had no catalogued class to be held against, WarpLink having been listed as identified and never written up while Mobzio is marketplace deeplinks for one regional seller set, and because the decision and spend tools are an operator surface rather than a developer one; the evidence tier is stated rather than implied, since the package is stdio only with no hosted endpoint and no tool was called. The five directory cards were re-probed rather than left as grouped holds: 442ball answered a keyless initialize 200 as 442ball 0.1.0 with 12 tools, forge-by-ui8 answered 401 with OAuth protected-resource metadata and fragments read and write scopes, paperjoy-01f7bf answered 401 on paperjoy.co/mcp behind 9 listed tools, eddyter stages a React editor into a codebase, and builders-in-fintech relisted and answered a keyless tools/list with 23 tools in 21,348 bytes where the guide recorded 19, so the guide count and FAQ were corrected in this commit. On /all, hologramxyz/avastudio-mcp answered 401 with 76 tool annotations in its listing snapshot and was held on the ad creative class carried by AdMake and Adspy, and perisclaw-mcp answered 401 and was held on the read-only messaging archive slice carried by Kaption WhatsApp. Counts for the supplement: guide tree 1,085 entries before and 1,086 after.

Evening sweep November 4 2026, eleven hours after the midday pass, and the shape was the reverse of the midday read: the feeds barely moved and the directory did. mcpservers.org went from 19,344 to 19,515 on both reads through the reader proxy, 171 entries, and its newest page shared no slug with the thirty the midday pass dispositioned; 120 slugs were read across pages 1 to 4 and 113 were unledgered on a first slug pass. mcp.so produced 26 server objects with the newest at 2026-11-04T23:13:21Z (Actora MCP) and only 4 cards above the midday stamp. The submission window carried 17 items between #6746 Scrape.ly at 18:02:07Z and #6762 Emploist at 2026-11-05T03:51:45Z, read with bodies in one authenticated call, one of them #6761 AGNT an MCP client rather than a server, so the window is 16 arrivals. The finding of the pass is about crossref rather than about servers: the 171-entry wave reads as 113 new slugs and as a handful of new products, because the directory is ingesting a backlog while the product-name form of the same items was already dispositioned by the night pass (the -docs-mcp documentation fleet of Cartrelay, Hirelabs, Ziva.sh, Teddit.io, Echoly, Skael, Webclaw, Recl and Rainbrand; the theluckystrike calculator four; the antevo.ch four; the tidybytetools trio) and thirteen more match this window or the one before it directly. Two entries were catalogued and both were driven rather than quoted. ProveCart at https://api.provecart.com/mcp answered a keyless initialize 200 as provecart 1.0.2 with all 10 tools listed; provecart_scoreboard and provecart_certification_info were called live and returned real payloads while the three check tools refused with one sentence naming the integrator X-API-Key they need, so the check payload is schema-read and not measured. The three check tools compare what an agent built against the customer's structured mandate and return a signed MATCH, REVIEW or BLOCK before the payment, with a non-MATCH answer carrying the Agent Correction Format: a corrections array of dimension, action, expected, actual and reason, a retry budget and a sealed evidence pointer. The mandates are the substance, 18 fields on an order including max_total_price, merchant_allowlist, merchant_blocklist, max_quantity, variant_constraints, price_basis, expires_at and a period_budget with its own window, 26 on a booking including airport_substitution, date_flex_days, fare_terms and the connection limits, 17 on a reservation including time_tolerance_minutes, party_size_max and max_deposit. The scoreboard read live is the argument for the exam: two agents at 100.0 over 29 checks with certification CURRENT to 2027-02-02 and two audit probes at 13.8 and 11.1, with origin separating external, house and audit runs; 80 or above certifies, a pass is CURRENT for 90 days, renewal is a newly generated exam and a pass yields an Open Badges 3.0 credential under did:web:api.provecart.com. lookfirst at github.com/Aethelgard-Systems/lookfirst is Apache-2.0 and was installed here and driven: lookfirst 0.2.1 against a README that says 0.2.0 pre-1.0, and the offline demo run twice, the approval run returning status executed with approved_by elicitation:mcp and readback ok while the fake bank moved 1,250.00 to 1,129.50 EUR for a 120.50 EUR transfer, the denial run returning status denied with the channel named and the balance untouched, both exiting 0. Five behaviours earn the guide: the decision table fails closed with readOnlyHint allowing and every write, unannotated tool and unknown tool confirming while deny never executes; the approval is bound to the arguments by a per-call HMAC token and the preview's args_sha256 with a 403 on mismatch and a timeout treated as denial; the write is verified by read-back reported as ok, unklar or fehlgeschlagen in structuredContent.lookfirst; the log is an Ed25519 hash chain where verify-log walked 20 signed entries to OK and then returned TAMPERED at line 6 after the demo rewrote the decision entry; and the result is masked before the model sees it, the client receiving [[IBAN_...]] placeholders that resolve inside the gate while an invented one is refused. The limits are the vendor's own: pre-1.0 with 0 stars and no field record, an autonomous client can self-approve through elicitation unless confirm.elicitation is off and the page is isolated at the network level, the page has no login and is for 127.0.0.1, an HTTP token is authentication not encryption, Windows is untested, and the mask is a deterministic filter that misses split IBANs, zero-width text, Base64 secrets and db_password. Held with measurements: mailers-scan-api, one keyless scan_domain returning a score against maxScore 80 plus MX, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, rDNS and domain age at 60 requests an hour with no DNSBL leg, held on class behind how.is with its 17 checks, Mamba's fingerprint and Leadgen; the antevo.ch four dispositioned together, Tremor Watch held on the note that 35 of 176 volatility and equity pairs broke at 3.1x normal, the 184th most unsettled of 1,348 Fridays since 2001, against portfolio-specific risk carried by PairBook and openInvest, with a per-portfolio exposure call recorded as the promotion test; Antevo Trademark held behind Goalie and IP Defender; 1ToolRing on the data-aggregator class; workbook-tools-mcp behind the SheetsFinance spreadsheet slice; uptrack, invisit and pdf-a11y on their carried classes; and the four feed cards Actora, Arsen, Circles and Airport Pickups London held as one vertical each. Three antevo.ch paths answered 405 to a keyless initialize, so Tremor Watch was dispositioned on its published figures rather than a session. Counts: guide tree 1,099 directories before this pass and 1,101 after, 1,243 entries counting single-file guides before and 1,245 after.

Midday sweep November 5 2026, seven hours after the night pass, and the shape was flat on both named surfaces. The twelve-sitemap canonical came back at 19,513 server URLs, the same number as the 04:31 MST capture, with 2 additions and 2 removals where both removals pair exactly with an addition whose namespace prefix was dropped - ad/mcp-project-helper became mcp-project-helper and dg/pohoda-mcp became pohoda-mcp - so nothing entered or left the ecosystem in the window. The locale strip is now mandatory before any diff: 43,181 URLs carry the locale inline as /de/servers/ rather than /servers/de/, and a naive set difference reads that as 43,179 additions. mcp.so was parsed from a direct fetch at 172 cards with the newest at 2026-11-05T06:47:30Z, which is the night pass's own stamp, so the feed carried zero new cards; mcpservers.org /all refused every read again, 403 to a direct browser-agent fetch and 401 03 bad IP reputation through the reader proxy, which is now the standing condition rather than an incident. The submission queue was the whole window: 36 items from #6773 Desktop Steward to #6808 DataXAPI, read with bodies in one authenticated call, and 21 of them are one author's fleet, mambalabsdev from #6782 to #6802, covering an email verifier, a whois lookup, a Substack scraper, a Reddit thread scraper, a Threads keyword search, an ATS jobs feed, a LinkedIn jobs feed, a Product Hunt launches feed, recent funding rounds, an app-store review monitor, an AI answer visibility tracker and six list-builder tools, every one of them in a class the catalog already carries, so the fleet is held as one line under the single-author rule. One arrival was catalogued. Korzy MCP - https://api.korzy.co/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and registered as co.korzy/korzy 1.0.0 at 2026-11-05T13:41:35Z, and a keyless initialize returns 401 with 'Sign in or provide a valid Korzy credential', so the tier is documentation rather than a driven session. The sixteen read-only tools are read 